@startuml
title PayLink - Payment State Diagram (FR-10 to FR-13)
[*] --> Initiated

Initiated --> Rejected : validation fails / insufficient funds
Initiated --> FundsHeld : checks pass and hold succeeds
FundsHeld --> SentToBiller : biller request sent

SentToBiller --> Completed : biller confirms paid
SentToBiller --> Failed : biller refuses
SentToBiller --> Unknown : no response within 10 seconds

Unknown --> Completed : later callback / re-query says paid
Unknown --> Failed : later callback / re-query says refused
Unknown --> Unknown : no answer after 1, 5 and 15 minute re-queries\nkeep funds held; wait for callback/reconciliation

Failed --> Refunded : release held funds

Completed --> [*]
Rejected --> [*]
Refunded --> [*]

note right of Failed
  Failure release is recorded in the ledger.
  The brief's lifecycle then records Refunded.
end note

note right of Unknown
  Never refund automatically.
  Hold remains in place until the outcome
  is known from callback or reconciliation.
end note

note bottom of Completed
  Final Payment state.
  A customer refund request creates a separate
  Refund record; Payment stays Completed.
end note
note bottom of Rejected
  Final state.
end note
note bottom of Refunded
  Final state.
end note
@enduml
